On 3rd October 2024, the Provisional Report with more details on demographic
and socio-economic data was launched by the Rt. Honourable Prime Minister.
That report had a clerical error on  tribe/ethnic population for figures from the
2014 Census, which generated heated debate and public outrage.
vi) Release of the final report on 31st December 2024.
vii) Dissemination of subject -specific thematic Census reports, policy briefs  and
area maps, among others, by June 2025.
1.3 The Census 2024 Final Results
The total population of Uganda was 45,905,417 persons with an average annual
growth rate of 2.9 percent as shown in Table 1.3. More findings from the Census can
be found in the NPHC 2024 Final Report – Volume 1 (Main) on the UBOS website
(https://www.ubos.org)
